Z||000012||Bazooka||10-06-2001||04:48 PM||||ds21,  The Vector W2 Twin Turbo was an Exotic Sports Limited Production car first offered in 1990. Gerald Wiegert and the Engineers of the Vector Aeromotive Corporation composed the 'state of the art' designs, which included an all Aluminum Twin Turbo Charged Engine dynoed at over 600 hp, Two Garrett H-3 Tirbochargers with Water Cooled Housings, High Efficiency Air to Air Intercooler, Semi-Monocoque chassis, Hybrid Composite of Carbon Kevlar Body, Heads-Up Instrumentation (Aircraft Type Menu-Driven Reconfigurable Electroluminescent Display), and countless other features. The first established base price of $178,000 increased to $250,000 within a year. Performance results included 0-60 time of 3.9 seconds, 1/4 mile at 11.8 seconds at 128 mph, Top Speed was 212 miles per hour. Vector was a Limited Production Car that was built in Wilmington, California for about 3 years until Lamborghinni bought it and tried to meld their designs into its Diablo.    <BR>*******************************<BR>Originally posted by ds21:<BR>[B]Looks Cool!<BR>Another car I've always been in love with is the Vector. Although I now think the W8 looks dated, well it did come out in the 70's! Back in about 92 I went to the winter CES show in Vegas and low and behold they had a Vector WX3 on display now that would be the perfect car for a Fiero Kit, similar to a Diablo but originally an American car! <BR>Just think of it The only other American Mid-engine Sports car as a kit for an American Mid-engine Sports car!<BR>Now That Would Be Cool!!!<BR>***********************************<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||ds21||10-06-2001||10:30 PM||||Good Research Bazooka, yeah I was always tempted to go down to their plant in Wilmington, at the time I lived about 30 min. away. And I suppose I should have said that the W8 was based on the W2 from the 70's (very close) the reason I like the WX3 is because it looks more modern and was still American, when it was sold and they came out with the M12 it wasn't American anymore. <BR>And now Mr. Wiegert has his new company to sell vaporware, base in Wilmington again, this time JetBikes hey he's looking for investors.||||reg||14
